<%# locals: (lead: nil, question: nil) %>
<%#
  What the four ranks mean and where to read them: one question and its
  answer, rendered inside the page's About This Report (or How This Page
  Works) list. Shared by every pipeline page so the ranks are described once;
  `lead` and `question` let a page that colours its rows --
  /mentoring/convert-prospectives is a table -- say what its own colouring
  means instead.
%>
<dt><%= question || "What do the ranks mean?" %></dt>
<dd>
  <%= lead || "Each team ranks a person from 1 to 4: 1 is above average, 2 average, 3 below average and 4 a flag. " \
              "Select a name: the gray line under it in the history lists every team's latest rank with its " \
              "year, and each year's entry and each training session carries its rank as a chip." %>
  Ranks:
  <span class="inline-flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 align-middle">
    <%= intake_rank_badge(Intake::FLAG) %>
    <%= intake_rank_badge(Intake::BELOW_AVERAGE) %>
    <%= intake_rank_badge(Intake::ABOVE_AVERAGE) %>
    <%= intake_rank_badge(Intake::AVERAGE) %>
  </span>
</dd>
